From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:37:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thermal: Add the Samsung Exynos9820 TMU

The thermal management unit of the Exynos9820 comes as two blocks, TOP
and SUB, each with its own registers, interrupt and bus clock.  Their
probes belong to the firmware on the APM: the vendor kernel asks it for
the temperature of five zones over the ACPM protocol and never reads a
temperature from the blocks.

Describe each block as its own node, with the ACPM interface the zones
are read through and the firmware zone number as the sensor specifier.
The zones and their numbers are the firmware's: the three CPU clusters
belong to TOP, the GPU and the ISP to SUB.

samsung,exynos-thermal.yaml describes TMUs the kernel programs itself,
with one sensor per node; here the sensors are served by the firmware
and addressed by zone number, hence a schema of their own.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml       | 76 +++++++++++++++++++
 MAINTAINERS                                   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..9c5a8423f19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Samsung Exynos9820 Thermal Management Unit
+
+maintainers:
+  - Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
+
+description: |
+  The thermal management unit of the Exynos9820 comes as two blocks, TOP
+  and SUB, each with its own registers, interrupt and bus clock and with
+  several temperature probes.  The firmware running on the APM owns the
+  probes, groups them into zones and reports the zones over the ACPM
+  protocol.  The zone numbers are the firmware's and span both blocks:
+
+    TOP block: 0 - big CPU cluster, 1 - middle CPU cluster,
+               2 - little CPU cluster
+    SUB block: 3 - GPU, 4 - ISP
+
+  Each block also has a hardware trip that removes the power at the
+  temperature programmed into it, without going through software.
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: thermal-sensor.yaml#
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    enum:
+      - samsung,exynos9820-tmu-top
+      - samsung,exynos9820-tmu-sub
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  "#thermal-sensor-cells":
+    const: 1
+    description:
+      The firmware zone number, one of those listed above for the block.
+
+  samsung,acpm-ipc:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The ACPM firmware interface the zones are read through.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - clocks
+  - "#thermal-sensor-cells"
+  - samsung,acpm-ipc
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9820.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
+
+    thermal-sensor@10090000 {
+        compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-tmu-top";
+        reg = <0x10090000 0x800>;
+        interrupts = <GIC_SPI 478 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+        clocks = <&cmu_peris CLK_GOUT_PERIS_TMU_TOP_PCLK>;
+        #thermal-sensor-cells = <1>;
+        samsung,acpm-ipc = <&acpm_ipc>;
+    };
diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index caddf06892d..b61f121a1a8 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -24003,6 +24003,7 @@ L:	linux-samsung-soc@vger.kernel.org
 S:	Maintained
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9820-clock.yaml
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml
+F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/samsung,exynos9820-tmu.yaml
 F:	arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820*
 F:	drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c
 F:	drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-exynos9820.c
